An original game. No names, characters, maps, models, sounds or code from
any other game or franchise.

Art and sound
- Models come from the per-style asset library
  (@netforge/asset-library): CC0 1.0 models by Kenney (Mini
  Characters, Blaster Kit, Space Kit, Car Kit), each pack listed with its
  source URL and licence verification in that package's NOTICE and
  manifest/packs.json. The files are fetched and built, never committed
  here; the build copies only the models this game uses.
- Fallback shapes (client/library.ts) are generated from three.js
  primitives; all textures are drawn on a canvas at load; all sounds are
  synthesized with WebAudio oscillators (client/audio.ts).

Dependencies (unmodified, via npm)
- three.js 0.186.1 (https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js), MIT.
- nipplejs 1.0.4 (https://github.com/yoannmoinet/nipplejs), MIT.
- @netforge/engine and @netforge/engine-sim (this repository);
  see their NOTICE files (bitECS MPL-2.0, Rapier Apache-2.0, Colyseus MIT,
  zod MIT).

Patterns (ideas only)
- The arena shooter genre's general mechanics (twin-stick aim, weapon
  loadouts, respawns, frag limits, health drops, a scoreboard). Mechanics,
  not expression; no level, weapon, character or text was copied from any
  game.
- Lag compensation for hitscan as described in Valve's public Source
  multiplayer networking write-up (ideas only; implemented in the Net Forge
  room server and engine-sim's arena seam).
- Hit-stop, screen shake and damage numbers as described in common
  game-feel talks and articles (e.g. "Juice it or lose it", GDC 2012).
